{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"length","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","reasoning_content":"We need count binary strings length 14 that avoid forbidden substrings \"000\" and \"111\". So no three consecutive same bits. Count sequences of length n with no run of 3 identical bits. This is classic recurrence. Let a_n be number of valid strings length n. We can use DP with states: last run length and last bit. Let's compute quickly.\n\nDefine dp[n][b][k] where b in {0,1} last bit, k run length 1 or 2. For n=1: dp[1][0][1]=1, dp[1][1][1]=1. For n>1: transition: if add same bit, only if k=1 -> new k=2; if k=2 cannot add same bit. If add opposite bit, new k=1.\n\nWe can compute iteratively.\n\nLet's compute using Python mentally? Let's do table.\n\nInitialize for n=1:\ndp1(0,1)=1\ndp1(1,1)=1\nothers 0.\n\nn=2:\nFrom dp1(0,1)=1: add 0 -> k=2 => dp2(0,2)+=1; add 1 -> dp2(1,1)+=1\nFrom dp1(1,1)=1: add 1 -> dp2(1,2)+=1; add 0 -> dp2(0,1)+=1\n\nSo dp2:\n(0,1)=1\n(0,2)=1\n(1,1)=1\n(1,2)=1\n\nn=3:\nFrom each state:\n\nState (0,1)=1: add 0 -> (0,2)+=1; add1 -> (1,1)+=1\nState (0,2)=1: add 0 not allowed; add1 -> (1,1)+=1\nState (1,1)=1: add1 -> (1,2)+=1; add0 -> (0,1)+=1\nState (1,2)=1: add1 not allowed; add0 -> (0,1)+=1\n\nCompute totals:\n(0,1): from (1,1) and (1,2) each 1 => 2\n(0,2): from (0,1) 1 =>1\n(1,1): from (0,1) and (0,2) =>2\n(1,2): from (1,1) =>1\n\nCheck also any other? none.\n\nn=4:\nStart with dp3 values.\n\nState (0,1)=2: add0 -> (0,2)+=2; add1 -> (1,1)+=2\nState (0,2)=1: add0 not; add1 -> (1,1)+=1\nState (1,1)=2: add1 -> (1,2)+=2; add0 -> (0,1)+=2\nState (1,2)=1: add1 not; add0 -> (0,1)+=1\n\nTotals:\n(0,1): from (1,1) 2 + (1,2)1 =3\n(0,2): from (0,1)2 =2\n(1,1): from (0,1)2 + (0,2)1 =3\n(1,2): from (1,1)2 =2\n\nn=5:\nState (0,1)=3: add0 -> (0,2)+=3; add1 -> (1,1)+=3\nState (0,2)="}}],"created":1790951936,"model":"C:\\Users\\d2j3\\Documents\\Codex\\2026-09-10\\napraw\\outputs\\moon-native\\models\\gpt-oss-20b-MXFP4.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b